#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:19
msgid ""
"Actions provide a structured way for ROS nodes to handle long-running tasks "
"with feedback. This tutorial describes how to define and build a custom "
"action interface in a package. After following these steps, you will be able "
"to create and verify a reusable action definition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:27
msgid "**Goal:** Define an action in a ROS 2 package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:29
msgid "**Tutorial level:** Intermediate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:31
msgid "**Time:** 5 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:35
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:38
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:40
msgid ""
"You learned about actions previously in the :doc:`Understanding-ROS2-Actions/"
"Understanding-ROS2-Actions` tutorial. Like the other communication types and "
"their respective interfaces (topics/msg and services/srv), you can also "
"custom-define actions in your packages. This tutorial shows you how to "
"define and build an action that you can use with the action server and "
"action client you will write in the next tutorial."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:47
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:49
msgid ""
"You should have :doc:`ROS 2 <../../../../Get-Started/Installation>` and "
"`colcon <https://colcon.readthedocs.org>`__ installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:51
msgid ""
"You should know how to set up a :doc:`workspace <../../../client-libraries/"
"Working-with-Client-Libraries/Creating-A-Workspace/Creating-A-Workspace>` "
"and create packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:53
msgid ""
"Remember to :doc:`source your ROS 2 installation <../../../../Get-Started/"
"Configuring-ROS2-Environment>` first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:56
msgid "Tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:59
msgid "1 Creating an interface package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:63
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:125
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:198
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:65
msgid ""
"$ mkdir -p ~/ros2_ws/src # you can reuse an existing workspace with this "
"naming convention\n"
"$ cd ~/ros2_ws/src\n"
"$ ros2 pkg create --build-type ament_cmake --license Apache-2.0 "
"custom_action_interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:71
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:132
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:204
msgid "macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:73
msgid ""
"$ mkdir -p ~/ros2_ws/src\n"
"$ cd ~/ros2_ws/src\n"
"$ ros2 pkg create --build-type ament_cmake --license Apache-2.0 "
"custom_action_interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:79
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:139
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:210
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:81
msgid ""
"$ md \\ros2_ws\\src\n"
"$ cd \\ros2_ws\\src\n"
"$ ros2 pkg create --build-type ament_cmake --license Apache-2.0 "
"custom_action_interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:87
msgid ""
"``custom_action_interfaces`` is the name of the new package. Note that it "
"is, and can only be, a CMake package, but this doesn't restrict in which "
"type of packages you can use your actions. The ``--build-type ament_cmake`` "
"flag is largely optional when creating a new ROS 2 package but we are "
"including it here for completeness. You can create your own custom "
"interfaces in a CMake package, and then use it in a C++ or Python node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:94
msgid ""
"It is good practice to keep ``.msg``, ``.srv``, and ``.action`` files in "
"separate packages from the nodes that use them. This makes it easier to "
"reuse the interface definitions across different packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:99
msgid "2 Defining an action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:101
msgid "Actions are defined in ``.action`` files of the form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:103
msgid ""
"# Request\n"
"---\n"
"# Result\n"
"---\n"
"# Feedback"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:111
msgid ""
"An action definition is made up of three message definitions separated by "
"``---``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:113
msgid ""
"A *request* message is sent from an action client to an action server "
"initiating a new goal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:114
msgid ""
"A *result* message is sent from an action server to an action client when a "
"goal is done."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:115
msgid ""
"*Feedback* messages are periodically sent from an action server to an action "
"client with updates about a goal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:117
msgid "An instance of an action is typically referred to as a *goal*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:119
msgid ""
"Say we want to define a new action \"Fibonacci\" for computing the "
"`Fibonacci sequence <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fibonacci_number>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:121
msgid ""
"Create an ``action`` directory in our ROS 2 package "
"``custom_action_interfaces``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:127
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:134
msgid ""
"$ cd custom_action_interfaces\n"
"$ mkdir action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:141
msgid ""
"$ cd custom_action_interfaces\n"
"$ md action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:146
msgid ""
"Within the ``action`` directory, create a file called ``Fibonacci.action`` "
"with the following contents:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:148
msgid ""
"int32 order\n"
"---\n"
"int32[] sequence\n"
"---\n"
"int32[] sequence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:156
msgid ""
"The goal request is the ``order`` of the Fibonacci sequence we want to "
"compute, the result is the final ``sequence``, and the feedback is the "
"``sequence`` computed so far."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:159
msgid "3 Building an action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:161
msgid ""
"Before we can use the new Fibonacci action type in our code, we must pass "
"the definition to the rosidl code generation pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:163
msgid ""
"This is accomplished by adding the following lines to our ``CMakeLists.txt`` "
"before the ``ament_package()`` line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:165
msgid ""
"find_package(rosidl_default_generators REQUIRED)\n"
"\n"
"rosidl_generate_interfaces(${PROJECT_NAME}\n"
"  \"action/Fibonacci.action\"\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:173
msgid "We should also add the required dependencies to our ``package.xml``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:175
msgid ""
"<buildtool_depend>rosidl_default_generators</buildtool_depend>\n"
"\n"
"<member_of_group>rosidl_interface_packages</member_of_group>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:181
msgid ""
"We should now be able to build the package containing the ``Fibonacci`` "
"action definition:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:183
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ros2_ws # Change to the root of the workspace\n"
"$ colcon build # Build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:188
msgid "We're done!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:190
msgid ""
"By convention, action types will be prefixed by their package name and the "
"word ``action``. So when we want to refer to our new action, it will have "
"the full name ``custom_action_interfaces/action/Fibonacci``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:193
msgid ""
"We can check that our action built successfully with the command line tool. "
"First source our workspace:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:200
msgid "$ source install/local_setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:206
msgid "$ source install/local_setup.console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:212
msgid "$ call install\\local_setup.bat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:216
msgid "Now check that our action definition exists:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:218
msgid "$ ros2 interface show custom_action_interfaces/action/Fibonacci"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:222
msgid "You should see the Fibonacci action definition printed to the screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:225
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Creating-an-Action.rst:227
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, you learned the structure of an action definition. You "
"also learned how to correctly build a new action interface using "
"``CMakeLists.txt`` and ``package.xml``, and how to verify a successful build."
msgstr ""

